Fix compilation of the bundled PnMPI (MUST -> GTI -> PnMPI) on AArch64 with GCC.

In MPI_Pcontrol (PnMPI's wrapper.c), inline (PNMPI_PCONTROL_VARG) arguments
in the PnMPI Pcontrol format were accessed by casting the va_list to a pointer:

    start = (TRANSTYPE *)va_alist;

This assumes va_list is a plain pointer into the stack argument area. On
AArch64 (AAPCS64) va_list is a struct, so GCC rejects the cast and the build
fails. On x86_64 the cast compiles only because va_list is an array type, but
points at the va_list bookkeeping structure, not at the arguments.

Forwarding untyped variadic arguments cannot be done portably, so the VARG
case now prints a warning and returns PNMPI_ERROR instead.

MUST is not affected functionally: mustrun configures PnMPI with
'globalpcontrol typed 4042 pointer' (TYPED mode), which reads its argument
with va_arg and never reaches this code path. The INT, TYPED and PTR modes
are unchanged.

author: Felix Tomski (RWTH Aachen University)
diff -ruN MUST-v1.11.2.orig/externals/GTI/externals/PnMPI/src/pnmpi/wrapper.c MUST-v1.11.2/externals/GTI/externals/PnMPI/src/pnmpi/wrapper.c
--- MUST-v1.11.2.orig/externals/GTI/externals/PnMPI/src/pnmpi/wrapper.c	2026-11-01 22:30:35.101125354 +0100
+++ MUST-v1.11.2/externals/GTI/externals/PnMPI/src/pnmpi/wrapper.c	2026-11-01 22:30:35.155611798 +0100
@@ -1043,7 +1043,17 @@
         }
       else
         {
-          start = (TRANSTYPE *)va_alist;
+          /* VARG: Forwarding the inline arguments requires va_list to be a
+           * plain pointer into the stack argument area. This does not hold on
+           * register-based ABIs like x86_64 and AArch64 (where va_list is a
+           * struct and the cast does not compile), so report an error instead.
+           * Use PNMPI_PCONTROL_PTR to pass arguments as a buffer. */
+          WARNPRINT("PNMPI_PCONTROL_VARG is not supported, use "
+                    "PNMPI_PCONTROL_PTR instead");
+          va_end(va_alist);
+          pnmpi_reset_return_address();
+          pnmpi_reset_function_address();
+          return PNMPI_ERROR;
         }
       leni = (size + sizeof(TRANSTYPE) - 1) / sizeof(TRANSTYPE);
 
